From: Linux psX contributors <noreply@ps4-linux>
Subject: [PATCH] ps4: initialize UART slots as unregistered

The APCIE UART setup is disabled, but removal still checks serial_line.
Zero-initialized slots appear to own ttyS0. Initialize every slot to the
existing negative sentinel before any setup or failure cleanup.

This is equivalent to the small fix already present in the comparison
reference c14cfac43067332e0376f389b3ddbc83b1cc0ca4 by rmuxnet; record that
reference rather than importing its surrounding controller rewrite.
No Aeolia hardware teardown acceptance is claimed.
---
diff --git a/drivers/ps4/ps4-apcie.c b/drivers/ps4/ps4-apcie.c
--- a/drivers/ps4/ps4-apcie.c
+++ b/drivers/ps4/ps4-apcie.c
@@ -512,16 +512,17 @@
 
 	sc = kzalloc(sizeof(*sc), GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!sc) {
 		dev_err(&dev->dev, "apcie_probe(): alloc sc failed\n");
 		ret = -ENOMEM;
 		goto disable_dev;
 	}
 	sc->pdev = dev;
+	memset(sc->serial_line, -1, sizeof(sc->serial_line));
 	pci_set_drvdata(dev, sc);
 
 	// eMMC ... unused?
 	sc->bar0 = pci_ioremap_bar(dev, 0);
 	// pervasive 0
 	sc->bar2 = pci_ioremap_bar(dev, 2);
 	// pervasive 1 - misc peripherals
 	sc->bar4 = pci_ioremap_bar(dev, 4);
